--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn driver deck -- dynamic run: chain under a regular Airy wave, 10 s
-- Same held-fairlead chain as dynamic_chain_held.dat, here with a regular (linear Airy) wave. The
-- waves keyword adds the Airy wave kinematics to the Morison drag plus a Froude-Krylov / buoyancy
-- wetting load at each element, so the fairlead/anchor tensions oscillate about the still-water
-- values. Studless chain, 50 m depth. waves = airy H=2.0 m T=8.0 s dir=0 deg.
